      "writtenOn": "2019-07-10T14:48:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack!\n\nyes, logically, we only need CONFIG_ISH_PM_AONTASK for ish-aon-bin. \nI tried below rules (very simple and clean): \n\nish-aon-out\u003d$(out)/aontaskfw\nish-aon-bin-$(CONFIG_ISH_PM_AONTASK)\u003d$(ish-aon-out)/$(ish-aon-name).bin\nish-aon-elf\u003d$(ish-aon-out)/$(ish-aon-name).elf\nish-aon-lds\u003d$(ish-aon-out)/$(ish-aon-name).lds\n\t\n...\nPROJECT_EXTRA+\u003d$(ish-aon-bin-y)\n...\n\n$(ish-aon-bin-y): $(ish-aon-elf)\n\t$(call quiet,elf_to_bin,EXTBIN )\n\t\n$(ish-aon-elf): $(ish-aon-lds) $(ish-aon-objs)\n\t$(call quiet,ish_aon_elf,LD     )\n\t\n$(ish-aon-lds): chip/$(CHIP)/aontaskfw/ish_aontask.lds.S\n\t-@ mkdir -p $(@D)\n\t$(call quiet,lds,LDS    )\n...\n\nbut always get below warnings (everything works good, just have warning messages when make): \n\nchip/ish/build.mk:58: warning: overriding recipe for target \u0027build/arcada_ish/aontaskfw/ish_aontask.elf\u0027\nchip/ish/build.mk:58: warning: ignoring old recipe for target \u0027build/arcada_ish/aontaskfw/ish_aontask.elf\u0027\nchip/ish/build.mk:61: warning: overriding recipe for target \u0027build/arcada_ish/aontaskfw/ish_aontask.lds\u0027\nchip/ish/build.mk:61: warning: ignoring old recipe for target \u0027build/arcada_ish/aontaskfw/ish_aontask.lds\u0027\n\nnot very understand why these warning happens, so, I still keep using CONFIG_ISH_PM_AONTASK for \u0027ish-aon-elf\u0027 and \u0027ish-aon-lds\u0027, then no any warnings.\n\non the other hand, we only want define valid targets (elf, lds) when CONFIG_ISH_PM_AONTASK defined, so using CONFIG_ISH_PM_AONTASK for \u0027ish-aon-elf\u0027 and \u0027ish-aon-lds\u0027 is also make sense.",
